### Virtual File System (VFS) Abstraction

The VFS abstraction will map user sessions to isolated directory sandboxes. This will prevent users from accessing files outside their designated sandbox.

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Security.AccessControl;

public class VirtualFileSystem
{
    private readonly string _rootPath;

    public VirtualFileSystem(string rootPath)
    {
        _rootPath = rootPath;
    }

    public string MapUserToSandbox(string userName)
    {
        var sandboxPath = Path.Combine(_rootPath, userName);
        if (!Directory.Exists(sandboxPath))
        {
            Directory.CreateDirectory(sandboxPath);
            // Set ownership and permissions for the sandbox directory
            var directoryInfo = new DirectoryInfo(sandboxPath);
            var directorySecurity = directoryInfo.GetAccessControl();
            directorySecurity.SetOwner(new NTAccount(userName));
            directoryInfo.SetAccessControl(directorySecurity);
        }
        return sandboxPath;
    }
}
```

### Audit Logging Subsystem

The audit logging subsystem will record file access and transfer metrics. We will use the Serilog library to implement this.

```csharp
