# Modular Distributed SQL Query Execution Engine in C#

## Overview

The following implementation provides a basic structure for a modular distributed SQL query execution engine in C#. It includes three main components: 
- Network Exchange Operator: responsible for buffering and routing data partitions between nodes.
- Hash Aggregation Operator: groups records in memory.
- Disk Spill Manager: spills intermediate hash tables to disk when memory limits are exceeded.

## Network Exchange Operator

This component will handle the exchange of data between nodes. It will use a buffering mechanism to ensure efficient data transfer.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Threading;

public class NetworkExchangeOperator
{
    private readonly object _lock = new object();
    private readonly Queue<byte[]> _outputQueue = new Queue<byte[]>();
    private readonly Queue<byte[]> _inputQueue = new Queue<byte[]>();
    private readonly int _maxOutputBufferSize;
    private readonly int _maxInputBufferSize;

    public NetworkExchangeOperator(int maxOutputBufferSize, int maxInputBufferSize)
    {
        _maxOutputBufferSize = maxOutputBufferSize;
        _maxInputBufferSize = maxInputBufferSize;
    }

    // Enqueue data to be sent over the network
    public void EnqueueOutput(byte[] data)
    {
        lock (_lock)
        {
            if (_outputQueue.Count >= _maxOutputBufferSize)
            {
                // If the buffer is full, block until space is available
                Monitor.Wait(_lock);
            }
            _outputQueue.Enqueue(data);
            Monitor.Pulse(_lock);
        }
    }

    // Dequeue data received from the network
    public byte[] DequeueInput()
    {
        lock (_lock)
        {
            if (_inputQueue.Count == 0)
            {
                // If the buffer is empty, block until data is available
                Monitor.Wait(_lock);
            }
            byte[] data = _inputQueue.Dequeue();
            Monitor.Pulse(_lock);
            return data;
        }
    }

    // Inject data into the input queue for local processing
    public void InjectInput(byte[] data)
    {
        lock (_lock)
        {
            if (_inputQueue.Count >= _maxInputBufferSize)
            {
                // If the buffer is full, block until space is available
                Monitor.Wait(_lock);
            }
            _inputQueue.Enqueue(data);
            Monitor.Pulse(_lock);
        }
    }
}
```

## Hash Aggregation Operator

This component will perform hash aggregation on the data. It will group records in memory based on the specified key columns.

```csharp
